OL,3,GNEWSAUK falls silent to mark Armistice
OL,4,ADay
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe UK has fallen silent on Armistice
OL,7,FDay, commemorating the end of World War
OL,8,FOne and to remember those who have died
OL,9,Fin conflicts.
OL,11,FA national remembrance service took
OL,12,Fplace at the Cenotaph in London, with a
OL,13,Ftwo-minute silence observed at 11:00
OL,14,Fduring ceremonies across England,
OL,15,FScotland, Wales and Northern Ireland.
OL,17,FDefence Secretary Wes Streeting laid a
OL,18,Fwreath at the Cenotaph, which was also
OL,19,Fattended by senior military figures,
OL,20,Fchildren and cadets.
OL,23,APub: 11-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBWales NewsC Reg TVFClean Feed
